Art Willis <nhplayer@trantor.nospam.com> writes:

[pudding farming and collecting the drops]

> Can anyone give the probability of an artifact as a death
> drop item?

In most cases, it's the probability of any randomly generated object
a) being a weapon (which will depend on where you are: 10% for most of
the dungeons) and b) being artifactified; if a weapon is generated
which has an artifact of its type that doesn't currently exist, it has
a 1/20 chance of the latter.

> Is it related to the experience value of the monster, or is one just
> as likely from a newt as from a black pudding?

Only the size of the monster matters (and whether it can leave a
corpse; and Kops don't have a death-drop at all). Tiny and small
monsters cannot death-drop most bulky items; all artifacts are bulky
for this purpose, so only medium or larger monsters can drop them.

> Does alignment figure into the calculations
> at all? Are chaotic artifacts also possible?

No and yes.

> Come to think of it, I do have Sting. Don't remember if it was a
> death drop or just something I found randomly in the dungeons.  Can
> any of the other quest artifacts ever show up as a death drop? I
> could go for the PYEC or the staff of misspelling.

Sting isn't a Quest Artifact, and can be randomly generated. No Quest
Artifacts (or Excalibur) can be randomly generated; see art1-343.txt,
and look at the 'r' symbols in the GENER column.

